  "articleBody": "When you're diving into a remodel, especially in areas like Denver, Centennial, or Aurora, electrical work is a huge piece of the puzzle. It's not just about flipping a switch; it's about making sure your electrician talks to the plumbing and HVAC teams. This coordination is super important because you don't want wires crossing pipes, literally! You might be asking, \"Who handles the permits and inspections?\" or \"What if they need to upgrade my electrical service?\" These are all valid concerns, and a good general contractor ensures these are all managed smoothly. The key is to get everyone on the same page early on. Overlaying drawings, identifying 'clash zones' where different systems might compete for space, and having regular meetings are all part of the process. Especially when you're doing something like a kitchen or bath remodel, where loads can be complex, or if you're dealing with dense routing, having a qualified professional is critical. You want someone who understands the timing for rough-in and those staged inspections. HH Remodeling LLC can be that single point of contact, ensuring all these pieces come together correctly and safely.",
